# Direct Recruit - Apple App Store Deployment Checklist

## Phase 1: PWA Foundation
[x] Create manifest.json in frontend root
[x] Create app icons:
    [ ] icon-180.png (Apple Touch Icon)
    [ ] icon-192.png (Android/PWA)
    [ ] icon-512.png (PWA install)
    [ ] icon-1024.png (App Store - no transparency, no alpha)
[x] Create iOS splash screens for all device sizes
[x] Add meta tags to ALL HTML files (40+ pages):
    - <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    - <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent">
    - <meta name="theme-color" content="#0a1128">
    - <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icons/icon-180.png">
    - <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json">
[x] Create service-worker.js for offline caching

## Phase 2: Capacitor Setup
[x] Initialize npm in project root: npm init -y
[x] Install Capacitor: npm install @capacitor/core @capacitor/cli @capacitor/ios
[x] Initialize Capacitor: npx cap init "Direct Recruit" com.directrecruit.app
    - domain is "directrecruit.net"
[ ] Configure capacitor.config.ts with webDir and server URL
[ ] Add iOS platform: npx cap add ios
[ ] Configure Info.plist permissions (camera, photo library if needed)

 https://www.macincloud.com
## Phase 3: Xcode & Build (Requires Mac)
[ ] Install Xcode from Mac App Store
[ ] Open project: npx cap open ios
[ ] Add Apple Developer account in Xcode
[ ] Set Bundle Identifier: com.directrecruit.app
[ ] Set deployment target (iOS 14.0+ recommended)
[ ] Add app icons in Assets.xcassets
[ ] Configure LaunchScreen.storyboard

## Phase 4: Apple Developer Account
[ ] Enroll in Apple Developer Program ($99/year)
    URL: https://developer.apple.com/programs/enroll/
[ ] Create App ID in Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles
[ ] Create Development provisioning profile
[ ] Create Distribution provisioning profile

## Phase 5: App Store Connect
[ ] Create new app in App Store Connect
[ ] Set app name: Direct Recruit
[ ] Set primary category: Sports
[ ] Set secondary category: Social Networking
[ ] Prepare screenshots:
    [ ] 6.7" display (iPhone 14 Pro Max)
    [ ] 6.5" display (iPhone 11 Pro Max)
    [ ] 5.5" display (iPhone 8 Plus)
[ ] Write app description (max 4000 chars)
[ ] Write promotional text (max 170 chars)
[ ] Add keywords (max 100 chars)
[ ] Add privacy policy URL
[ ] Add support URL
[ ] Complete age rating questionnaire

## Phase 6: Code Adjustments
[ ] Test deep links work correctly
[ ] Verify status bar handling on notched devices
[ ] Test keyboard behavior in all forms
[ ] Test all modals in WebView
[ ] Verify Socket.IO works through Capacitor WebView
[ ] Test file uploads (camera, photo library)
[ ] Test media playback (highlight videos)

## Phase 7: Testing
[ ] Test on physical iPhone (not just simulator)
[ ] Test on iPhone SE (small screen)
[ ] Test on iPhone 14/15 (standard)
[ ] Test on iPhone Pro Max (large screen)
[ ] Test on iPad (if universal app)
[ ] Test offline behavior
[ ] Test push notifications (if implemented)
[ ] Test all user roles (hsplayer, collegeplayer, transferplayer, hscoach, collegecoach, other)

## Phase 8: Submission
[ ] Archive build in Xcode (Product → Archive)
[ ] Validate app in Organizer
[ ] Upload to App Store Connect
[ ] Fill in "What's New" section
[ ] Submit for App Review
[ ] Monitor for review feedback (usually 24-48 hours)

